# Credential-bearing files, named explicitly.
#
# These replace two blanket rules (`connectors/PythonIntegration/*.txt` and
# `*.md`) that were added a day after the files they meant to hold back had
# already been committed. .gitignore does not untrack, so those rules never
# removed anything — README.md, CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and the rest stayed
# tracked and public — while still being broad enough to silently swallow a
# legitimate new top-level .md or .txt.
#
# This is a backstop, not the mechanism: what reaches this repository is decided
# by the allowlist in connectors/tools/sync_public_mirror.py in the source repo.
**/HOW_TO.txt
**/.pypirc
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example